lines=['# real-go2 branch: odometry check on the lab bag','',f"Repository branch **real-go2**, pinned commit `{commit}`. Lab source: `/home/jain/go2_bags/go2_20261018_173219`, 217.353 s. Operator returned approximately to the starting position and heading.",'','| Path | Estimated horizontal return offset | Estimated heading change |','|---|---:|---:|',f"| Raw vendor | {raw['horizontal_return_offset_m']:.3f} m | {raw['heading_return_change_deg']:.2f} degrees |",f"| Repo default, yaw_scale=0.9814 | **{cor['horizontal_return_offset_m']:.3f} m** | {cor['heading_return_change_deg']:.2f} degrees |",f"| Repo optional Point-LIO with guarded vendor bridge | {hy['horizontal_return_offset_m']:.3f} m | {hy['heading_return_change_deg']:.2f} degrees |",'','Return offsets include real placement differences and estimator error; no surveyed ground-truth drift is claimed. All endpoint comparisons use the same developer URDF IMU lever arm and quiet windows, 2.6–3.6 s and 210–216 s.','', '![Comparison](results/comparison.png)','','## Default path','',f"[real_mapping.launch.py]({url}unitree_go2_real/launch/real_mapping.launch.py) defaults to lio=false. [real_bridge.yaml]({url}unitree_go2_real/config/real_bridge.yaml) supplies yaw_scale=0.9814. [real_tf_bridge.py]({url}unitree_go2_real/scripts/real_tf_bridge.py) rotates each vendor translation step into the body frame and reintegrates it using scaled heading increments. The value is the repository author's published setting; it was not fitted to this bag.",'',f"The original on_odom callback was run offline on all {raw['samples']:,} source vendor messages with ROS side effects replaced by passive sinks. The identity setting yaw_scale=1.0 reproduces the original pose values to {raw['identity_callback_matches_original_pose_max_absolute_difference']:.3g} maximum absolute difference. Default correction improves this lab route's return from 1.083 m to 0.155 m.",'','## Optional Point-LIO path and guard','',f"The original [LioInput adapter]({url}unitree_go2_real/scripts/lio_input.py), [Point-LIO profile]({url}unitree_go2_real/config/point_lio_go2.yaml) and point_lio_unilidar package were tested without source changes. The adapter uses vendor-deskewed clouds transformed back into body coordinates, LiDAR gyro with startup bias subtraction, zero accelerometer input, and accumulation configured as con_frame_num=8. The branch's accumulator publishes the accumulated group on a following callback; its native LIO update cadence is therefore slower than the high-rate vendor output.",'',f"The guarded bridge accepted **{guard['accepted']}** LIO corrections, last at **{guard['last_accepted_source_s']:.3f} s**. After the four-second recording gap it rejected **{guard['rejected']}** corrections, first at **{guard['first_rejection_source_s']:.3f} s**; no later LIO correction was accepted. Its thresholds are 0.3 m and 5 degrees against the previous correction. The first rejection in bridge.log is about 1.96 m / 104.7 degrees. Thus this optional Point-LIO also fails across the data gap. The bridge protects the published pose by holding its last accepted correction and continuing vendor odometry.",'','The optional output keeps vendor z, roll and pitch. Its returned height is not an independent LIO vertical-accuracy measurement. A protected hybrid output must not be interpreted as healthy raw Point-LIO after the gap.','','## Recovery and verification limits','',a['method'],'',f"All {hy['holds']['start']['samples']} initial-hold and {hy['holds']['finish']['samples']} final-hold source messages were verified present in the bridge's saved callback sequence. Correction M is identity throughout the initial hold and unchanged throughout the final hold, so rerunning the original on_odom callback recovers those endpoint outputs exactly. Full optional LIO/hybrid trajectory arrays were not saved and are not reconstructed or plotted. The plot shows full paths only for the default/raw modes, plus the recovered optional final endpoint.",'',f"The bridge audit reaches {guard['last_lio_source_s']:.3f} s and contains {guard['accepted']+guard['rejected']} LIO correction events. It received {guard['bridge_source_messages']} / {guard['source_messages_total']} vendor messages. Missing source times: `{guard['bridge_missing_vendor_source_times_s']}` s, outside the selected endpoint holds. Full observer-based cloud/IMU delivery verification is unavailable for this interrupted optional observer; the earlier complete lab replay has its own delivery audit. Acquired source gaps were preserved, not filled.",'',f"Original source and active application/calibration hashes unchanged: **{a['source_and_application_files_unchanged']}**. Build and replay stayed in a separate review workspace / localhost-only DDS domain 210. No commands were replayed. Existing active TF and mapping setup were not changed.",'','## Straight-distance cross-check','','The same original default yaw correction was also checked on the earlier recordings, using their existing quiet holds:','','| Bag | Raw vendor 3 m / 5 m | Corrected vendor 3 m / 5 m |','|---|---:|---:|']
straight={}
